    "forbiddenName": {
      "from": "framework-manifest.json",
      "field": "product_name_retired"
    },
    "_forbiddenNameExemptNote": "The shipped files whose JOB is to name retired identifiers: the manifest that records them, the validator that detects them, and this manifest (whose exempt rows below must spell what they exempt). The carve-out is per-DEST-PATH and per-NAME — a file may declare only the identifiers it has business declaring, and anything else still rejects there. The workshop's internal name appears in no list: no shipped file declares it. example-receipt.html is deliberately ABSENT — its exemption covers autobiography (dogfoodRefs), never the old name.",
    "forbiddenNameExempt": {
